IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`
IMPORT `sg-groups`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), ss 201B and 201C (Part 6, Division 1): the audit committee of a listed company, and when directors need not lay
-- financial statements before a private company that need not hold an annual general meeting.
-- "Listed" is s 4(1) "listed", "private company" is s 4(1) "private company", "related corporation" is s 4(1) / s 6 (the keel's sg-groups.l4 answers it, and
-- is imported here for that one call): each is taken as an input named for the fact, the s 6 answer through the keel's function.
-- Whether a company need not hold an annual general meeting because of s 175A(1) is a later wave's: an input named for the fact.
-- Subsection (10) is shown deleted (Act 36 of 2014).

§ `Section 201B: the acts of the regulative rules`

DECLARE `s 201B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 201B(1) have an audit committee`
    `s 201B(4) appoint new members of the audit committee to make up the minimum number of 3`
    `s 201B(6) appear before the audit committee when required to do so`
    `s 201B(7) convene a meeting of the audit committee on the auditor's request`
    `s 201B(9) describe in the directors' statement the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee`

DECLARE `s 201B(5) function` IS ONE OF
    `s 201B(5)(a)(i) review with the auditor the audit plan`
    `s 201B(5)(a)(ii) review with the auditor the auditor's evaluation of the system of internal accounting controls`
    `s 201B(5)(a)(iii) review with the auditor the auditor's audit report`
    `s 201B(5)(a)(iv) review the assistance given by the company's officers to the auditor`
    `s 201B(5)(a)(v) review the scope and results of the internal audit procedures`
    `s 201B(5)(a)(vi) review the financial statements and any consolidated financial statements submitted to the committee, and thereafter submit them to the directors`
    `s 201B(5)(b) nominate a person or persons as auditor, despite anything contained in the constitution or under section 205`
    `s 201B(5) some other function`

§ `Section 201B(1): the duty to have an audit committee`

-- src:18404 | 201B.—(1) Every listed company must have an audit committee.
@ref s 201B(1) (src:18404-18404)
GIVEN `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(1) the company must have an audit committee` MEANS
    IF `the company is a listed company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "every listed company" and says nothing of any other company (a scope limit with no "only": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection: no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201B(1) (src:18404)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201B act`
`s 201B(1) a listed company must have an audit committee` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 201B(1) have an audit committee`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 201B(1) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the listed company did not have an audit committee" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 201B(2): who sits on the audit committee`

-- src:18406 | (2) An audit committee must be appointed by the directors from
-- src:18407 | among their number (pursuant to a resolution of the board of
-- src:18408 | directors) and must be composed of 3 or more members of whom a
-- src:18409 | majority must not be —
-- src:18414 | (a) executive directors of the company or any related
-- src:18415 | corporation;
-- src:18417 | (b) a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or adopted son or
-- src:18418 | daughter or adopted daughter of an executive director of
-- src:18419 | the company or of any related corporation; or
-- src:18421 | (c) any person having a relationship which, in the opinion of
-- src:18422 | the board of directors, would interfere with the exercise of
-- src:18423 | independent judgment in carrying out the functions of an
-- src:18424 | audit committee.
@ref s 201B(2) (src:18406-18424)
GIVEN `the audit committee was appointed by the directors from among their number` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the appointment was made pursuant to a resolution of the board of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members of the audit committee` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members who are within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(2) the audit committee is appointed and composed as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF    `the audit committee was appointed by the directors from among their number`
       AND `the appointment was made pursuant to a resolution of the board of directors`
       AND `the number of members of the audit committee` AT LEAST 3
       AND (`the number of those members who are within paragraph (a), (b) or (c)` TIMES 2) AT MOST `the number of members of the audit committee`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "An audit committee must be appointed by the directors from among their number (pursuant to a resolution of the board of directors) and must be composed of 3 or more members of whom a majority must not be — (a) executive directors ...; (b) a spouse, parent, brother, sister, son or adopted son or daughter or adopted daughter of an executive director ...; or (c) any person having a relationship which, in the opinion of the board of directors, would interfere with the exercise of independent judgment" (a duty not met: the provision's own question; "a majority must not be" read as: those within (a) to (c) are at most half)

§ `Section 201B(3): the chairperson`

-- src:18426 | (3) The members of an audit committee must elect a chairperson
-- src:18427 | from among their number who is not an executive director or
-- src:18428 | employee of the company or any related corporation.
@ref s 201B(3) (src:18426-18428)
GIVEN `the person is a member of the audit committee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an executive director of the company or of any related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of the company or of any related corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(3) the person is eligible to be elected chairperson of the audit committee` MEANS
    IF    `the person is a member of the audit committee`
       AND (NOT `the person is an executive director of the company or of any related corporation`)
       AND (NOT `the person is an employee of the company or of any related corporation`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The members of an audit committee must elect a chairperson from among their number who is not an executive director or employee of the company or any related corporation" (a closed requirement: the provision's own question)

§ `Section 201B(4): making up the number of members`

-- src:18430 | (4) If a member of an audit committee resigns, dies or for any other
-- src:18431 | reason ceases to be a member with the result that the number of
-- src:18432 | members is reduced below 3, the board of directors must, within
-- src:18433 | 3 months of that event, appoint such number of new members as may
-- src:18434 | be required to make up the minimum number of 3 members.
@ref s 201B(4) (src:18430-18434)
GIVEN `the day the member resigns, dies or for any other reason ceases to be a member` IS A DATE
      `the number of members of the audit committee after that event` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 201B(4) the last day for the board of directors to appoint new members` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the audit committee after that event` LESS THAN 3
    THEN JUST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the day the member resigns, dies or for any other reason ceases to be a member` 3 Months)
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the case where "the number of members is reduced below 3" and is silent on a committee that still has 3 or more

@ref s 201B(4) (src:18430-18434)
GIVEN `the day the member resigns, dies or for any other reason ceases to be a member` IS A DATE
      `the number of members of the audit committee after that event` IS A NUMBER
      `the day the board of directors appoints the new members` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(4) the board of directors has appointed new members in time` MEANS
    IF `the number of members of the audit committee after that event` AT LEAST 3
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of the case where "the number of members is reduced below 3" and is silent on a committee that still has 3 or more
    ELSE IF `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the member resigns, dies or for any other reason ceases to be a member` `the day the board of directors appoints the new members` 3 Months
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the board of directors must, within 3 months of that event, appoint such number of new members as may be required" (a period the text fixes in its own words: the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (a))

-- The clock counts days from the event; the deadline is the number of days from the event to the end of the 3 months.
@ref s 201B(4) (src:18430-18434)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
      `the number of days from the event to the end of the 3 months` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201B act`
`s 201B(4) the board of directors must within 3 months appoint new members to make up the minimum number` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201B(4) appoint new members of the audit committee to make up the minimum number of 3`
    WITHIN `the number of days from the event to the end of the 3 months`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the board of directors did not appoint new members to make up the minimum number of 3 within 3 months"

§ `Section 201B(5): the functions of an audit committee`

-- src:18436 | (5) The functions of an audit committee are —
-- src:18438 | (a) to review —
-- src:18440 | (i) with the auditor, the audit plan;
-- src:18442 | (ii) with the auditor, the auditor’s evaluation of the
-- src:18443 | system of internal accounting controls;
-- src:18445 | (iii) with the auditor, the auditor’s audit report;
-- src:18447 | (iv) the assistance given by the company’s officers to the
-- src:18448 | auditor;
-- src:18450 | (v) the scope and results of the internal audit procedures;
-- src:18451 | and
-- src:18453 | (vi) the financial statements of the company and, if it is a
-- src:18454 | parent company, the consolidated financial
-- src:18455 | statements, submitted to it by the company or the
-- src:18456 | parent company, and thereafter to submit them to the
-- src:18457 | directors of the company or parent company; and
-- src:18462 | (b) to nominate a person or persons as auditor, despite
-- src:18463 | anything contained in the constitution or under section 205,
-- src:18465 | together with such other functions as may be agreed to by the audit
-- src:18466 | committee and the board of directors.
@ref s 201B(5) (src:18436-18466)
GIVEN function IS A `s 201B(5) function`
      `the audit committee and the board of directors have agreed that the committee performs it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(5) the function is one of the functions of an audit committee` MEANS
    CONSIDER function
    WHEN `s 201B(5) some other function` THEN
        IF `the audit committee and the board of directors have agreed that the committee performs it`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The functions of an audit committee are — (a) to review ...; (b) to nominate ..., together with such other functions as may be agreed to by the audit committee and the board of directors" (a function neither listed nor agreed)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§ `Section 201B(6) and (7): the auditor and the committee`

-- src:18470 | (6) The auditor has the right to appear and be heard at any meeting
-- src:18471 | of the audit committee and must appear before the committee when
-- src:18472 | required to do so by the committee.
@ref s 201B(6) (src:18470-18472)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(6) the auditor has the right to appear and be heard at any meeting of the audit committee` MEANS
    IF `the person is the auditor of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the right is given to "the auditor" and the subsection is silent on anyone else

@ref s 201B(6) (src:18470-18472)
GIVEN `the person is the auditor of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the audit committee requires the auditor to appear before it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(6) the auditor must appear before the committee` MEANS
    IF `the person is the auditor of the company` AND `the audit committee requires the auditor to appear before it`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must appear before the committee when required to do so by the committee" (a failed "when": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection: no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201B(6) (src:18470-18472)
GIVEN `the name of the auditor` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201B act`
`s 201B(6) the auditor must appear before the committee when required to do so` MEANS
    PARTY Auditor `the name of the auditor`
    MUST `s 201B(6) appear before the audit committee when required to do so`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 201B(6) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Auditor `the name of the auditor` BECAUSE "the auditor did not appear before the audit committee when required to do so" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

-- src:18474 | (7) Upon the request of the auditor, the chairperson of the audit
-- src:18475 | committee must convene a meeting of the committee to consider any
-- src:18476 | matters the auditor believes should be brought to the attention of the
-- src:18477 | directors or shareholders.
@ref s 201B(7) (src:18474-18477)
GIVEN `the auditor has requested the chairperson of the audit committee to convene a meeting to consider matters the auditor believes should be brought to the attention of the directors or shareholders` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(7) the chairperson must convene a meeting of the audit committee` MEANS
    IF `the auditor has requested the chairperson of the audit committee to convene a meeting to consider matters the auditor believes should be brought to the attention of the directors or shareholders`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the request of the auditor, the chairperson of the audit committee must convene a meeting of the committee" (a failed "upon": counted as "where", the ruling of 2026-11-05 on delegated definitions, item (c))

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection: no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201B(7) (src:18474-18477)
GIVEN `the name of the chairperson` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201B act`
`s 201B(7) the chairperson must convene a meeting of the committee on the auditor's request` MEANS
    PARTY Individual `the name of the chairperson`
    MUST `s 201B(7) convene a meeting of the audit committee on the auditor's request`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 201B(7) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Individual `the name of the chairperson` BECAUSE "the chairperson did not convene a meeting of the audit committee on the auditor's request" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 201B(8): the committee's own procedure`

-- src:18479 | (8) Each audit committee may regulate its own procedure and in
-- src:18480 | particular the calling of meetings, the notice to be given of such
-- src:18481 | meetings, the voting and proceedings thereat, the keeping of minutes
-- src:18482 | and the custody, production and inspection of such minutes.
@ref s 201B(8) (src:18479-18482)
GIVEN `the matter is part of the audit committee's own procedure, in particular the calling of meetings, the notice to be given of them, the voting and proceedings at them, the keeping of minutes or the custody, production and inspection of minutes` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(8) the audit committee may regulate the matter` MEANS
    IF `the matter is part of the audit committee's own procedure, in particular the calling of meetings, the notice to be given of them, the voting and proceedings at them, the keeping of minutes or the custody, production and inspection of minutes`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is of "its own procedure"; the subsection is silent on any matter that is not procedure

§ `Section 201B(9): the audit committee in the directors' statement`

-- src:18484 | (9) Where the directors of a company or of a parent company are
-- src:18485 | required to make a statement under section 201(16) and the company
-- src:18486 | is a listed company, the directors must describe in the statement the
-- src:18487 | nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee
-- src:18488 | pursuant to subsection (5).
@ref s 201B(9) (src:18484-18488)
GIVEN `the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(9) the directors must describe the audit committee's functions in the statement` MEANS
    IF `the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` AND `the company is a listed company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the directors of a company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16) and the company is a listed company, the directors must describe in the statement the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b))

@ref s 201B(9) (src:18484-18488)
GIVEN `the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is a listed company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the statement describes the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee pursuant to subsection (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(9) the directors' statement describes the audit committee's functions as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the directors of the company or of a parent company are required to make a statement under section 201(16)` AND `the company is a listed company`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of a listed company whose directors are required to make a statement under section 201(16) and is silent on any other
    ELSE IF `the statement describes the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee pursuant to subsection (5)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the directors must describe in the statement the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee pursuant to subsection (5)" (a duty not met: the provision's own question)

-- No time limit and no consequence inside the subsection: no trace can show a breach (NOTES.md, Rules with no breach path).
@ref s 201B(9) (src:18484-18488)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 201B act`
`s 201B(9) the directors of a listed company must describe the audit committee's functions in the statement` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 201B(9) describe in the directors' statement the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    -- no LEST: s 201B(9) states no time for this duty, so a breach needs a standard from elsewhere (Interpretation Act 1965 s 52: "with all convenient speed"); dropped clause: LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not describe in the directors' statement the nature and extent of the functions performed by the audit committee" (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

§ `Section 201B(11): who is an executive director`

-- "a director who is not an executive director ... is a reference to a director who is not an employee of, and does not hold any other office of profit in, the company or in any
-- related corporation of that company in conjunction with his or her office of director and his or her membership of any audit committee, and any reference to an executive director
-- is to be read accordingly." Whether the other corporation is a related corporation is s 6's question, answered by the keel's function from the fact that s 6 deems it related.
-- src:18494 | (11) Any reference in this section to a director who is not an
-- src:18495 | executive director of a company is a reference to a director who is not
-- src:18496 | an employee of, and does not hold any other office of profit in, the
-- src:18497 | company or in any related corporation of that company in conjunction
-- src:18498 | with his or her office of director and his or her membership of any
-- src:18499 | audit committee, and any reference to an executive director is to be
-- src:18500 | read accordingly.
@ref s 201B(11) (src:18494-18500)
GIVEN `the person is an employee of the company or holds any other office of profit in the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is an employee of, or holds any other office of profit in, another corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201B(11) the director is an executive director` MEANS
    IF    `the person is an employee of the company or holds any other office of profit in the company`
       OR (`the person is an employee of, or holds any other office of profit in, another corporation`
           AND `s 4(1) "related corporation" the other corporation is a related corporation of the corporation` `the other corporation is deemed to be related to the company by virtue of section 6` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a director who is not an executive director ... is a reference to a director who is not an employee of, and does not hold any other office of profit in, the company or in any related corporation of that company" (a definition: a director who is neither is not an executive director)

§ `Section 201C: private companies that need not hold an annual general meeting`

-- src:18502 | When directors need not lay financial statements before
-- src:18503 | company
-- src:18505 | 201C.—(1) The directors of a private company need not comply
-- src:18506 | with the requirement in section 201 to lay before the company at its
-- src:18507 | annual general meeting financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18512 | statements of the company if the company need not hold an annual
-- src:18513 | general meeting because of section 175A(1).
@ref s 201C(1) (src:18502-18513)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201C(1) the directors need not lay financial statements before the company at its annual general meeting` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a private company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "the directors of a private company" and says nothing of any other company
    ELSE IF `the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)`
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "need not comply with the requirement in section 201 to lay before the company at its annual general meeting financial statements ... if the company need not hold an annual general meeting because of section 175A(1)" (a failed "if": marginal reading (a), NOTES.md; the other reading is NOTHING, since the relief is grant-like)

-- src:18517 | (2) Where the financial statements or consolidated financial
-- src:18518 | statements are not laid before the company at its annual general
-- src:18519 | meeting under subsection (1), the reference in section 207(1) to
-- src:18520 | financial statements required to be laid before the company in general
-- src:18521 | meeting is to be read as a reference to the documents required to be
-- src:18522 | sent to persons entitled to receive notice of general meetings of the
-- src:18523 | company under section 203(1).
@ref s 201C(2) (src:18517-18523)
GIVEN `the financial statements or consolidated financial statements are not laid before the company at its annual general meeting under subsection (1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 201C(2) the reference in section 207(1) is read as a reference to the documents sent under section 203(1)` MEANS
    IF `the financial statements or consolidated financial statements are not laid before the company at its annual general meeting under subsection (1)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the financial statements or consolidated financial statements are not laid before the company at its annual general meeting under subsection (1), the reference in section 207(1) ... is to be read as a reference to the documents required to be sent ... under section 203(1)" (a failed "where": the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (b), applied to a deeming)
